---
description: Communicate engineering work in plain and concise language
alwaysApply: true
---

# Plain language

- Lead with the outcome, decision, or blocker.
- Prefer short, direct sentences and concrete terms.
- Explain jargon only when it helps the reader act.
- Separate observed evidence from inference and uncertainty.
- Report exact validation and avoid claims broader than the evidence.
- Use only enough headings, lists, and detail to make the response easy to scan.
